\title{UNIX Files}
\date{2026-07-09T12:17:03Z}

\p{Open a file with the \code{open} [syscall](A5S6). Must be called with the following:}
\ul{
  \li{\code{eax} contains system call number.}
  \li{\code{ebx} contains pointer to string with name of file to open.}
  \li{\code{ecx} contains the options for opening the file.}
  \li{\code{edx} contains permissions used to open the file.}
}

\p{Pointers to all command line arguments are stored on the stack.}
\ul{
  \li{Number of arguments is stored at #{8}(\code{esp}),}
  \li{Name of program at #{12}(\code{esp}),}
  \li{Arguments at #{16}(\code{esp}) on.}
}
\p{These are the \code{argv} array in C.}

\p{
\pre\verb<<<|
fd (int) → fd table → struct file → struct inode
   per-process         "open file        the actual file
                       description"      (one per file)
<<<
}
